WEBVTT

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:04.690
Oh, Ei-chan!

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.060
Welcome back!

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.940
Thanks.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.170
It feels like it's been forever!

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.570
So how was Florida?

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.320
Did you have fun?

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.130
Yeah, I had a great time.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:16.620
Wh-What?

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.120
You don't look that different.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.860
My appearance wouldn't 
change in just two weeks.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.820
Oh? Listen to you.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.370
Coach Aoi!

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.240
I had a great experience, thanks to you.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.630
I don't need gratitude or anything.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.240
You came home stronger, right?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.630
Yes.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.250
With that excess energy gone, 
his form is much smoother.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.900
That's proof he gained some 
confidence over there.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.090
Sending him to America was the right choice.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:21.130
But frankly, I think he's still a long way 
from winning the All-Japan Junior.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.910
I know, but...

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.090
That's his goal.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.510
From a normal perspective,

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.400
given his lack of experience, 
Maruo-kun winning is near impossible.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:33.040
That's why I called you.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.620
Well, I'll do everything I can.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.960
We have two and a half months until the 
Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.420
Yukichi, starting tomorrow, we'll 
bump up both your regular regimen

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.410
and your strength-building regimen.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.520
R-Right!

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.200
Maruo-kun, you'll start a 
muscle-building regimen

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.310
and strengthen the offensive control 
regimen you followed in Florida.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:57.490
We'll add other special regimens 
from there, so be ready.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.070
Okay.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.990
Two and a half months will 
go by before you know it.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.550
October  STC Cup Kanagawa Tournament 
November  All-Japan Junior Kanto Region Indoor Qualifier
January  All-Japan Junior Indoor Qualifier 
March  Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament 
July  Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament 
August  All-Japan Junior Tennis Tournament

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.900
We don't have a second to waste.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.080
Right!

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.080
Takuma's Decision

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.820
You're hitting harder than before, Bro.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.040
Really?

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.170
That's one of the things I learned in Florida.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.690
Sorry for the wait, Ei-chan!

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.090
Ready to go?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.130
Yeah.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.460
Okay, we're off!

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.600
See you tomorrow.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.600
Good practice today!

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.730
It's so cold. Want to take a bus?

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.710
No, let's walk home.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.610
I want to hear all about Florida.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.020
Hey, have you seen Natsu?

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.670
Nat-chan just left with Bro.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.960
With Maruo?

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.620
Those two seem to be 
pretty close lately, don't they?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.120
What'd you do that for, Takuma-san?!

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:56.030
You've gotten a lot better, Ei-chan.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.130
Really?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.130
I'm really glad.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.490
<i>I-It's been so long, I feel 
like I might start grinning!</i>

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.030
So, did you have any trouble living abroad?

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.960
Oh... There was a Japanese 
guy there named Atsushi-san.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.660
He helped me out a lot, so it was okay.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.950
I see!

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:19.280
We were all worried about whether 
you'd get by okay over there.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.240
We thought you'd never fit in, 
since you're so serious.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.430
Well, it wasn't all fun all the time.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.790
I got into a losing habit at one 
point and couldn't win at all.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.560
A losing habit? What's that?

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.200
Huh? You've never been through that?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:39.800
Yeah... You don't seem like 
the type to think too deeply.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.930
I think deeply about things!

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.880
Uh, no, I didn't mean it that way!

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.660
I just thought maybe not thinking 
deeply was a way out of that habit.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.930
I think it's amazing!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.210
Well, okay, then...

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:55.940
And?

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.260
Oh... I played a match 
against Ike-kun over there,

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:03.020
and he told me that if I wanted to 
thank someone, I should thank you.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.570
You guys worked together 
somehow, didn't you?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.650
Ah... What could you mean by that?

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.070
Huh?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.060
You didn't ask Ike-kun to do something?

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.980
I don't remember.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:15.080
You do too remember!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.080
No idea what you mean.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.280
Well, whatever...

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.810
Thanks to that, I got to have 
a really good experience.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.090
Thanks.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.480
Sure!

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.090
How was So-chan? Good?

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.320
More than good. He clobbered me.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.710
Mentally, too.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:31.910
What did he do to you?!

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:36.100
What... well... he said 
you were his fiancée...

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.100
Me? So-chan's fiancée?

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.110
You believed him, didn't you?

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.760
It's not totally a lie, though.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.610
Wh-What?!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.180
It was when we were little, of course!

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.160
That whole, "When we grow up, 
I'm gonna marry So-chan" thing!

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.730
Kids like to say stuff like that!

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:54.620
<i>But I don't like to hear it at all!</i>

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.630
So-chan was the boy closest to me.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:01.060
I didn't even really know 
what marriage meant,

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.140
but I kept saying that.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:09.720
No Pedestrian Crossing
Please use the pedestrian bridge to cross.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.940
When we started middle school, 
he was still my closest friend,

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.720
so I started to think it might really happen.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.720
<i>Middle school? That wasn't so long ago...</i>

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:17.100
When So-chan decided to go to America, I knew

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.810
that we made more sense as 
friends than as a couple.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:27.570
Does that... make you jealous?

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:28.450
Huh?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.700
Y-Yes! Of course it does!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.080
I-It does?

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.380
N-Nat-chan!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.470
I've always felt that I should tell you...

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:43.090
I...

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.860
I really...

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.250
li—

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.590
...think you're amazing.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.150
T-Takuma-san.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:56.100
Takuma...

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.340
Sh-Shall we go?

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:14.320
Y-Yeah.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.820
<i>I-I feel like I just had a 
perfect opportunity to win</i>

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.820
<i>and hit it straight into the net!</i>

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.070
<i>No! I did my best!</i>

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.840
<i>I took a step... No, half 
a step forward, for sure!</i>

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.360
<i>Don't panic... Don't panic!</i>

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.350
<i>He works faster than I expected.</i>

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.500
I really...

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:42.230
li—

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.460
<i>That bastard. I've known her for ten years.</i>

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.940
Takuma! Let's go to practice!

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.450
Game, set. Winner: Egawa.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.350
Egawa Takuma 
Ike Soji

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:58.360
I'm really glad I won today.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.250
I heard Egawa Takuma was sorely defeated.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.410
We can't restrict Ike Soji to Japan any longer.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.750
You're not gonna practice?

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.770
Huh?

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.570
Your injury's healed now, right?

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.030
You said you were gonna go pro.

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:17.980
Shut up!

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:25.990
<i>Are you doing okay?</i>

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:28.460
<i>You haven't been coming 
to practice much lately.</i>

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:31.070
<i>Coach Miura is really worried.</i>

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.840
<i>I'm worried, too.</i>

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.500
Takuma!

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.990
Oh, Takuma!

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.710
Thank goodness!

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.070
Your injury's better now, right?

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.000
I guess.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.750
Oh, hey! I'm gonna go to the 
same high school as you!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.840
You'd better start calling me 
"Takuma-senpai," then.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.270
What? I can't just start doing that now!

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.620
You're still Takuma, just like always.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:59.710
<i>I went to practice because 
Natsu was worried about me.</i>

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.780
<i>Just hitting serves was fun...</i>

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:06.850
<i>But I was still running away from going pro.</i>

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.360
<i>Am I going to run away without 
trying anything again?</i>

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:11.550
<i>No!</i>

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:18.370
<i>"How do you feel about Maruo?"</i>

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:24.370
That was fast!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:31.090
I like him. But I can't tell him yet, so keep it secret!

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.100
Out! Twenty push-ups!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.260
I screwed up again!

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.610
This is killing me!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:53.300
I understand that you guys 
feel like you're dying.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:56.030
But this is the only chance you 
have to push your bodies hard,

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.110
in these two and a half months 
before the tournament.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.880
If you're in danger, I'll stop you.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.120
So go as far as you can.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.210
Right!

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.620
Right...

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.920
We have a practice match this afternoon.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.260
Maruo-kun, I want you to challenge 
your opponent yourself.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:13.630
Him.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.630
Takuma-san?

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.090
But he turned me down before...

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.600
Are you okay with leaving 
it that way forever?

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.510
And your schedule from now on...

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.600
Um, excuse me!

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.100
I need to talk to Takuma-san.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.660
Maruo-kun...

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:34.070
All right. There's something 
I want to ask you, too.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:35.610
Come with me.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.370
Huh?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:42.820
U-Um—

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:43.530
You...

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.900
haven't told Natsu you like her yet?

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.380
So you were listening yesterday?

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:57.060
Idiot. Just so you know, 
it was a coincidence.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:57.850
Oh...

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:00.290
And? What happened after that?

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.640
Well, uh...

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.640
I-I haven't!

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.560
You haven't told her?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:08.850
No.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.680
I can't believe this.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:11.900
Yeah...

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:15.230
Um, was that really all you wanted to ask me?

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.740
<i>I'm talking about romance with Takuma-san?</i>

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.520
Yeah. I'm done.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:23.070
Um, there's something I 
want to say to you, too.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.330
Please... play a match against me!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.310
Takuma-san!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.750
It made sense that you
turned me down last time.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.750
But in order for me to go pro,

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:37.340
I can't lose any more matches from now on.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.110
The same way a pro like you would,

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:43.340
I have to show results in a 
match with my life on the line.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:46.360
So I beg of you, just one match!

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.560
Then I'll ask you this.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.850
Do you think you can beat me now?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:56.790
I don't know.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:01.110
But if I can't at least beat you, 
I can't become a pro.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.270
I see.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:06.620
If that's the case, I'll play you.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.450
What? Really?!

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.120
Well, I just happen to be

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.130
in the mood to crush you to pulp.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.740
Come to Court 1 at sundown.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.140
Hey, Takuma.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.390
Sorry to ask this of you, but thanks.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.390
Hello, Aoi-san.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.230
Go ahead and beat the hell out of him.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.780
Whose side are you on?

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.760
Takuma's ranked number 500 
in the world right now.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.490
The way you're going, you could 
shoot above him in no time.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.990
<i>500?!</i>

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:50.790
<i>Even Alex is only ranked 
number 890 in the world...</i>

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.290
Three-set match.

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.290
Takuma to serve.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:55.790
<i>A year and a half ago,</i>

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:59.000
<i>I didn't even know how far from me he was,</i>

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.010
<i>but I can't say things like that now.</i>

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.000
<i>I've grown, too.</i>

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.010
<i>I've believed in myself and 
sharpened my instincts.</i>

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:11.010
15-love.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.020
<i>What is this?!</i>

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:14.680
30-love.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.520
<i>This makes all the other serves I've 
ever been given seem like nothing!</i>

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:18.980
<i>They're that fast!</i>

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.270
40-love.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.010
<i>This is more than I expected.</i>

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:27.160
<i>If innate physical ability 
can be called talent,</i>

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.600
<i>there's no one else as blessed 
with talent as this.</i>

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.230
<i>He dragged his feet for a while,</i>

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:35.290
<i>but now that he's over it, 
this is what he's capable of.</i>

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:42.050
Game: Takuma. 1-0.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:45.090
<i>C-Can I break serve like this?</i>

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:48.260
<i>No, I can't think negatively.</i>

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.440
<i>All I have to do is hold my own serve.</i>

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.740
<i>Keep shots deep for the most part,</i>

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.780
<i>and watch my course on short shots.</i>

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.400
<i>He hits hard!</i>

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:08.570
<i>But I gained experience with that in Florida!</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.240
<i>Control!</i>

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.260
Good one.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.750
15-love.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:18.290
Yes!

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:22.420
<i>The control I learned in Florida 
works on Takuma-san, too!</i>

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:26.050
<i>So he goes on the attack without waiting 
around for an opportunity now.</i>

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:30.050
<i>Well, this is the guy who made it to the 
top of the juniors in under two years.</i>

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.560
<i>I thought he had no talent, but...</i>

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.970
Ei-chan!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.520
Did you decide to pick up tennis?

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.140
Huh?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:40.230
Oh, I haven't applied to join yet.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.020
Who are you?

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.900
Are you also looking to go pro?

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.110
Pro?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.610
That's none of your business.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.860
So for now, I'll cram as much 
training as I can into my schedule,

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:57.870
and see if it's truly impossible after that.

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:57.870
<i>Honestly, he was a really annoying kid.</i>

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.880
<i>But I have to admit he's 
evolved at an amazing speed.</i>

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.130
<i>Evolved at amazing speed...</i>

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.380
<i>He was the same way.</i>

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.890
<i>Ike Soji.</i>

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:14.930
<i>I thought there wasn't much difference 
in the talent we were born with,</i>

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:17.720
<i>but he surpassed me before I even knew it.</i>

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.470
<i>I've been told I should do this 
and that because I have talent,</i>

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.960
<i>but that doesn't really mean anything.</i>

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:29.440
<i>In the end, you, Ike, and I 
each have something different!</i>

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:32.880
<i>The only question is whether 
we can make a living with it!</i>

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:33.700
<i>Right?!</i>

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.700
15-all.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:39.610
Nat-chan, you're done already?

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:42.040
The national invitational is coming up soon.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.040
Oh, yeah. Good luck.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.870
Game: Takuma. 5-2.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.050
Takuma leads.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.290
The reason Takuma's been able 
to win in the pros lately

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.460
is definitely his serve.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:54.050
Yeah.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:58.600
The serve he loves so much that he couldn't stop 
practicing, even when he was out of form,

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.730
is vital to him in the professional world.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.300
It took him a long time, 
but he finally realized that.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.080
That's how he was finally able to become

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:10.070
the best server in Japan.

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:12.150
<i>When it's my serve,</i>

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.610
<i>he returns it easily, 
taking away my advantage,</i>

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.990
<i>so I don't get to use my control.</i>

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:19.790
<i>Takuma-san wins points easily 
with his powerful serves.</i>

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.100
<i>The game count is 5-2.</i>

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:25.310
<i>That deficit is the difference 
between our serves.</i>

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:28.820
<i>I want... I want a serve like that, too!</i>

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.350
<i>A serve that gives me a huge advantage!</i>

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:32.710
Time.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.230
<i>To play at the pro level,</i>

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:37.520
<i>even if you don't have power or confidence,</i>

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.780
<i>a strong serve is indispensable.</i>

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:40.930
<i>In that case...</i>

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:43.690
<i>I'll hit as hard as I can!</i>

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:49.200
Oh, he put a lot of power into that one.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.650
Has he realized it, then?

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:55.050
<i>Crap! I can't put too much power into these!</i>

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:57.100
<i>The stroke and rhythm are important, too.</i>

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:59.950
<i>And I'd say the higher I connect, the better!</i>

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.460
Double fault. Love-15.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.960
Damn it!

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:08.750
<i>I need to follow a rhythm</i>

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.960
<i>and put my whole body into that 
same point of contact...</i>

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:14.590
Fault.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.380
<i>It's not working!</i>

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:19.760
<i>But I can't win this match 
if my serve doesn't improve!</i>

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:22.770
Double fault. Love-30.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:27.260
Come on, are you trying to abandon 
this game for some serve practice?

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.410
Considering his chances of winning,

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:31.940
maybe this was the only way for him.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:34.610
I did want him to realize that,

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.160
but realizing it too well is a problem, too.

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:40.950
Double fault. Love-40.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:48.170
<i>All I can do is make up for my lack of height 
and power with efficient movements.</i>

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:52.170
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.670
Double fault.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.760
First set winner: Takuma.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.630
Count: 6-2.

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:01.750
<i>Little by little, it's getting better.</i>

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.780
<i>I wanted to hit some more, 
but I can't help that.</i>

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.490
<i>Instead, I'll take thorough 
notes of what I just did</i>

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.210
<i>and make my reason memorize it,</i>

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:10.810
<i>so I can move by instinct 
alone as soon as possible.</i>

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.690
Time.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:13.530
<i>It's my return game.</i>

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.190
<i>First, I need to watch his 
serve closely and return it!</i>

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.530
<i>He always tosses with the same rhythm,</i>

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:23.730
<i>and gathers power in his lower body by 
bending his knees at the same time.</i>

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.540
<i>The moment his knees extend,</i>

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.740
<i>right after that power is 
released to his upper body,</i>

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:30.730
<i>his shoulders begin the swing.</i>

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:32.930
<i>That power travels to his elbow,</i>

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.100
<i>then his wrist, like the flexing of a whip,</i>

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:38.000
<i>giving the racket speed 
as it keeps going higher.</i>

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.580
<i>Then, at the highest point, 
where it has the most speed,</i>

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.300
<i>he makes impact!</i>

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:44.560
15-love.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:46.560
<i>I was completely lost in watching it!</i>

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.560
<i>But I see it now!</i>

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:55.820
Out. 30-love.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.820
<i>I need to watch more closely!</i>

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.640
<i>He flexes like a whip,</i>

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:01.820
<i>and there's the crack!</i>

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:06.490
Out. 40-love.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.500
Damn it! Almost there!

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.890
<i>He's able to send them back now.</i>

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.500
<i>Actually, back then, too...</i>

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>A total rookie of only one month</i>

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.690
<i>managed to reach my serve.</i>

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:22.130
<i>Damn... This kid just never 
stops pissing me off!</i>

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:26.970
Go in!

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.480
Game: Takuma. 1-0.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.600
<i>Using the image burned in my 
mind of Takuma-san's serve,</i>

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.970
<i>what will my body do?</i>

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:38.460
<i>Okay!</i>

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.280
<i>Make my whole body flex...</i>

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:44.280
It made it!

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.290
<i>It's short! I can go for it!</i>

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.540
<i>Control!</i>

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:52.790
15-love.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:53.790
Yes!

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.500
<i>Not enough! Go faster!</i>

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:03.300
<i>Not bad. Keep the same image 
in mind for my second.</i>

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.500
15-all.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:12.000
<i>This speed isn't enough for my second serve.</i>

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.810
<i>This is how much difference 
a serve can make in a match!</i>

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.840
<i>I need a faster serve!</i>

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:19.160
<i>Flex not just my shoulder, elbow, and wrist,</i>

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:22.820
<i>but my waist, making my whole 
body move like a single whip!</i>

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.080
30-15.

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:28.600
Yes!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:30.830
Fault.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:34.250
<i>If I can't get enough speed 
on my second serve,</i>

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:35.670
<i>then put spin on it!</i>

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.840
<i>Or make it look that way, 
but keep it loose to be safe!</i>

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.920
<i>Yes! His timing was off!</i>

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:43.930
<i>Straight?</i>

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:46.550
<i>A drop shot!</i>

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:48.600
Whoa!

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.100
30-all.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:55.190
Takuma! I told you to use drop shots 
only when you have a greater advantage!

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.610
Desperate shots can become a habit!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.860
I know that!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.200
<i>I thought so! He did that because 
he didn't know what to do!</i>

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.190
<i>I have the advantage on my serve!</i>

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:07.010
<i>I can do this! Make the next serve fast!</i>

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.810
Stop right there.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.870
Let's call this match here.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:14.650
What?!

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:18.270
U-Um, how can you say that now?

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:21.500
Sorry, but I want you to call it off...
rather, put it on hold.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:23.620
Why?!

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:27.660
If you keep this up, I'm afraid 
you're going to hurt yourself.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:28.510
Huh?

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.880
Takuma-san, please wait!

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.520
I'm not hurt at all!

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:36.520
You don't have a choice. Aoi-san said so.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:41.150
Besides, it's not cancelled. Just on hold.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.510
I don't feel good about it, either.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:46.900
I'll continue this with you any time.

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:49.910
Sorry to do this after I asked you to play him.

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.910
It's fine. Thanks for the game.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.590
Come on, Coach Aoi!

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.240
Hey, calm down.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:59.510
I'll explain why I did it.

00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:31.950
All right.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:01.870
Oh, it's Shimizu-san.

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:03.570
You know her, Nat-chan?

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:06.130
Yeah. She's the first seed in 
the next women's tournament.

00:24:06.550 --> 00:24:10.010
I've been up against her four times 
in three years, but never won.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:11.970
<i>You</i> lost all four matches?!

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:15.180
I want to beat her just once 
before I go pro, if I can.

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:20.380
I didn't know you had an opponent 
like Nabae-kun is for me...

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.450
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.290 --> 00:24:25.020
First Encounter by Scouting

00:24:22.450 --> 00:24:24.200
"First Encounter by Scouting."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
